<figure class="runtime-map" aria-labelledby="runtime-map-title">
  <figcaption id="runtime-map-title"><span>LIFETIME NESTING</span><strong>The runtime closes platform objects before shared App state</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="runtime-map__timeline" aria-hidden="true"><span>startup</span><i></i><span>shutdown</span></div>
  <ol>
    <li class="core"><b>Core App</b><span>shared state</span></li>
    <li class="runtime"><b>Runtime App</b><span>event-loop owner</span></li>
    <li class="rt-surface"><b>Runtime Surface</b><span>platform container</span></li>
    <li class="surface"><b>Core Surface</b><span>terminal-session owner</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p>The headless runtime creates one pair of Surface objects during <code>run</code>. <code>terminate</code> destroys them before <code>App.destroy</code> checks that no core surfaces remain.</p>
</figure>
